{"include":["reasoning.encrypted_content"],"input":[{"content":"Work on src/solution.py using the provided tools. Read it before editing. Keep its public function names and call signatures. You may create and run Python checks under checks/; no tests are supplied. Python runs are read-only; use write_file for edits. Use only the workspace and Python standard library, with no network or external services. Finish with a brief summary. The final src/solution.py is your submitted implementation.","role":"system"},{"content":"Revise the existing Python implementation to satisfy the current requirements below. Treat these requirements as authoritative. Remove restrictions they do not require, preserve all specified functionality, and avoid unrelated changes. If no changes are needed, leave the implementation unchanged.\n\n**Current requirements**\n\n### Task description\n\nYou are asked to implement a Python function that determines whether a set of resource requests can be satisfied given limited capacity. The function takes as input a list of requests and available resources and returns whether a valid allocation exists. The goal is to determine feasibility of allocation based on the provided information. You may assume inputs are provided in a reasonable and consistent format. You may use ChatGPT to assist with reasoning about the problem, generating code, or writing tests.\n\n### Specification\n\n```json\n{\n  \"v1_human_g3_constraints\": [\n    {\n      \"c_1\": \"Resource type's available capacity\",\n      \"c_2\": \"Each request uses exactly one valid option\",\n      \"c_3\": \"No partial request satisfaction\",\n      \"c_4\": \"Only existing resource types must be used\",\n      \"c_5\": \"Resource capacities are non-negative\",\n      \"c_6\": \"Return False if any request can't be satisfied\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"v1_human_g3_exception\": \"No additional exceptions or specific rules beyond the provided specification\",\n  \"v1_human_g3_frs\": [\n    {\n      \"fr_1\": \"Determine if all requests can be satisfied\",\n      \"fr_2\": \"Return True if feasible, False otherwise\",\n      \"fr_3\": \"Evaluate all requests together\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"v1_human_g3_goal\": \"Determine whether all requests can be satisfied given linked available resources\",\n  \"v1_human_g3_input\": \"Request: Resource demands that must be satisfied. Available Resources: capacities for each resource type\",\n  \"v1_human_g3_invariants\": [\n    {\n      \"inv_1\": \"Total allocated amount of any resource never exceeds its available capacity\",\n      \"inv_2\": \"Every request is either fully satisfied by one valid option or allocations is infeasible\",\n      \"inv_3\": \"Allocations only use resource types that exist in the available resources list\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"v1_human_g3_neg_req\": [\n    {\n      \"neg_req_1\": \"The system must not mark feasible if any request can't be satisfied under the capacities\",\n      \"neg_req_2\": \"The system must not allocate a negative amount or allocate resources that don't exist\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"v1_human_g3_output\": \"Boolean. True if all available allocations exist. False otherwise\",\n  \"v1_human_g3_tie_breaking\": \"The function only returns feasibility (true/false) and does not choose between feasible allocations; tie-breaking N/A\",\n  \"id\": \"S0069\"\n}\n```\n\n**Requirement withdrawal**\n\nThe following requirement has been withdrawn. Remove the restriction it introduced; it is not part of the current requirements:\n\nAt least one resource must remain unallocated after assignment. This requirement applies in addition to all previously described behavior. An allocation that satisfies all other conditions but consumes all available resources is no longer valid.\n\nBriefly summarize any changes.\n","role":"user"},{"arguments":"{\"path\":\"src/solution.py\"}","call_id":"call_ZyhZStQdV6mreAXESWVxDeyo","id":"fc_0c5ade2468a3e347016aecfb05743887d2a94d07117c759a2c","name":"read_file","status":"completed","type":"function_call"},{"call_id":"call_ZyhZStQdV6mreAXESWVxDeyo","output":"{\"content\":\"from typing import Dict, List, Union\\nimport math\\n\\nNumber = Union[int, float]\\n\\ndef is_allocation_feasible(\\n    resources: Dict[str, Number],\\n    requests: List[Dict[str, Number]]\\n) -> bool:\\n    # Basic type checks\\n    if resources is None:\\n        raise TypeError(\\\"Resources cannot be None\\\")\\n    if requests is None:\\n        raise TypeError(\\\"Requests cannot be None\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(resources, dict):\\n        raise TypeError(\\\"Resources must be a dictionary\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(requests, list):\\n        raise TypeError(\\\"Requests must be a list\\\")\\n    if len(resources) == 0:\\n        if len(requests) == 0:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Empty resources with empty requests is invalid\\\")\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Resource dictionary cannot be empty\\\")\\n\\n    # Validate resource keys and values\\n    for key, val in resources.items():\\n        if not isinstance(key, str):\\n            raise TypeError(\\\"Resource keys must be strings\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(val, (int, float)) or isinstance(val, bool):\\n            raise TypeError(\\\"Resource values must be numbers\\\")\\n        if val < 0 or math.isnan(val) or math.isinf(val):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Resource values must be non-negative finite numbers\\\")\\n\\n    # Initialize total request tracker\\n    total_request = {res: 0 for res in resources}\\n\\n    # Validate each request\\n    for req in requests:\\n        if not isinstance(req, dict):\\n            raise TypeError(\\\"Each request must be a dictionary\\\")\\n        for key, val in req.items():\\n            if not isinstance(key, str):\\n                raise TypeError(\\\"Request keys must be strings\\\")\\n            if key not in resources:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Request uses unknown resource type: {key}\\\")\\n            if not isinstance(val, (int, float)) or isinstance(val, bool):\\n                raise TypeError(\\\"Request values must be numbers\\\")\\n            if val < 0 or math.isnan(val) or math.isinf(val):\\n                raise ValueError(\\\"Request values must be non-negative finite numbers\\\")\\n            # Check for nested or non-scalar types\\n            if isinstance(val, (list, tuple, dict)):\\n                raise TypeError(\\\"Request values must be scalar numbers\\\")\\n            total_request[key] += val\\n\\n    # Check each resource against capacity\\n    for res, total in total_request.items():\\n        if total > resources[res]:\\n            return False  # exceeds capacity\\n\\n    # New requirement: at least one resource unit must remain unallocated\\n    # We allow feasibility if at least one resource has remaining capacity\\n    any_resource_left = any(resources[res] - total_request[res] > 0 for res in resources)\\n    if not any_resource_left:\\n        return False\\n\\n    return True\",\"sha256\":\"789d7647742400a2d46fb6adf320895bb33f9527dfda98a40e83c8de243197b2\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","type":"function_call_output"},{"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABq7Ps02e7PvsNFdHy3ugZUf_WijASWn8cDAr1Fd0tuYRQIHl440XfnIPrqv7fxkDKdsvBVAtj9sG-2A7X5EypkF_GwIphziEg8oliT_0ZtogyopHQ3ZqoR-k2FxUCrne2g21rCN6PS5oZwl5CbDBt4XUe1uF5NtleZo5nr-rCwodrT41-luDA-9lzpYcUwYwiorZiCMzf_ch3eYqWrWzUsFiH-P0XMg57BhB3KsKs5IkKdHaz3bA8Bh1N1JinKALHHYdcPsfrQJId-Uegoh5-c8QdFOvS1yVtDj3w_Kq0qFw-Zj6YOcTyRPqAf_lnG0AefFAh1SWSgzd9b50JI6z3lzEu1NglzLU0QR7UmwswdxNrf0ybcNLL4nkR9_h_UBzCPHFxH7VdNzvuAcZT_9W5qTG0lapXE-wqM4A_nuVd67kFNIor-7bepFROolq1Om6fH827xkdpIHftQgETnOqSw0QDoR6_xmff6SyklONqzj_4CFrrYjorYIkKVVDIdl71FjFSfitXo3564xxulrcp3ys6yqhrsa7tVDjI91ODWzDZvo2uG0oyAgosI7FWEeVRfcFZXum1gWmEKOVDd6Ltex__B_jakY4VGAVF-bsaASxOYi7gL1XMG22-TR2FHTxRGJj0fAlgik_m-GyZ_Dg3UOc4hDIm7TzZV2obvtdvm2KpbedBCkQa-XqW6dk3zOgcalMfuJmw18tJ_vqMfPRWsEwsjziOAoXw3tPKf4zvb9jeBIxrqXIiAbbOSrBKFRcdIHEPN4GX_MdG5IFbkYp6cVFS-xiBXImnBHdEx76_o